    "problem_statement": "Jobs not being cancelled when returning CancelJob\n\n#### Description\n\nJobs that return `schedule.CancelJob` are no longer being automatically cancelled from the scheduler. The cancellation mechanism appears to be broken.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport schedule\n\ndef stop_job():\n    return schedule.CancelJob\n\n# Schedule a job that should cancel itself\nschedule.every().second.do(stop_job)\nprint(f\"Jobs before run: {len(schedule.jobs)}\")  # Should be 1\n\n# Run the job - it should cancel itself\nschedule.run_all()\nprint(f\"Jobs after run: {len(schedule.jobs)}\")   # Should be 0, but is 1\n```\n\nExpected output:\n```\nJobs before run: 1\nJobs after run: 0\n```\n\nActual output:\n```\nJobs before run: 1\nJobs after run: 1\n```\n\nThe job should be automatically removed from the scheduler when it returns `CancelJob`, but it remains scheduled."
